Binary feedback produced no strict repairs among the 24 tasks under either guide setting. Layered feedback repaired 18/24 tasks without the Fixer guide and 14/24 with it, corresponding to gains of 75.0 and 58.3 percentage points over binary feedback. The latest run therefore supports the value of layered diagnostics but not a complementary strict-success gain from the Fixer guide. With layered feedback, enabling the guide reduced candidate-level strict success from 12/12 to 8/12, left core-operator strict success unchanged at 6/8, and reduced the observed core-operator OOS edit rate from 12.5\% to 0.0\%. No condition repaired any of the four core autograd/optimizer tasks.

