\subsection{Verifier Signals and Final Fixer Capability}

\subsubsection{Signal Sanity under Controlled Faults}
\label{sec:signal-effectiveness}
\textbf{Design.}
We evaluated whether each verifier signal detects the fault class it is designed to expose. This experiment uses controlled fault injection rather than automatic repair. For each model and seed, we compare a PyTorch reference step with a \texttt{torch4ms} candidate under one of three injected conditions: an execution fault, a numerical fault, or a training fault. The evaluation uses four model families (CNN, MLP, Transformer, and tiny causal LM), three seeds per fault, and thresholds of $\Delta_{\mathrm{loss}}>0.02$, $\Delta_{\mathrm{grad}}>0.05$, and $\Delta_{\mathrm{param}}>0.03$.

